        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312-a1">

                <pb facs="0637" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg527"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 72.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from Le Moniteur of May</hi> 28, 1890.</head>
                <p>Hyppolite, President of Haiti, in view of articles 2 and 9 of the law of April
                    13, 1880, concerning martial law, on the advice of the council of the
                    secretaries of state, decrees that which follows: <list>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1. The decree of May 24,
                            1888, which declares martial law in the arrondissement of Port-au-Prince
                            is and remains revoked.</item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 2. The present decree shall be
                            printed, published, and executed under the diligence of the secretaries
                            of state, each in that which concerns him.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Done at the <placeName>
                            <placeName type="venue">National Palace</placeName> of <placeName
                                type="city">Port-au-Prince</placeName></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian haitian-republic" when="1890-05-28">the 28th of
                            May, 1890, the eighty-seventh year of independence</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hyppolite.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>By the President:</p>
                    <closer><signed><list>
                                <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mompoint, Jr.</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                        rendition="#italic">Secretary of War and Marine</hi>.</item>
                                <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">St. M. Dupuy</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                        rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Interior and of the
                                        Police General.</hi></item>
                                <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clement Haentgens</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                        rendition="#italic">Secretary of Agriculture and of Public
                                        Works</hi>.</item>
                                <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Le Chaud</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                        rendition="#italic">Secretary of Justice and
                                    Worship</hi>.</item>
                                <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. S. Rameau</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                        rendition="#italic">Secretary of Public
                                    Instruction.</hi></item>
                            </list></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
